  <h2>Use it in real life</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Your age and theirs:</b> Say your real age, then the age of two people in your family. <span class="ex">I am thirty-four. My sister is twenty-nine. My father is sixty-two.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Fictional phone number:</b> Use a made-up number, not private information. Read <span class="ex">555-0137</span> one digit at a time: <span class="ex">five five five, zero one three seven</span>. Say it again with <span class="ex">oh</span> for zero.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Prices at the store:</b> Point at three things and say the price. <span class="ex">This is fifteen dollars. That is forty dollars. The total is fifty-five dollars.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Room and address numbers:</b> Use real or invented information. <span class="ex">I live at number eighteen. My office is in room thirteen.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Listen and write:</b> Your teacher says a number between 0 and 100. Write the numeral. Then say a number for your teacher to write. Watch the <span class="ex">-teen / -ty</span> pairs.</div>

  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Final production: a one-minute number profile</h3>
    <p>Without reading the examples, give your teacher five pieces of information: an age, a price, a quantity, a room or address number, and a fictional phone number. Include one <span class="ex">-teen</span> number, one <span class="ex">-ty</span> number, and one joined number such as <span class="ex">forty-two</span>.</p>
    <p><strong>Success criteria:</strong> the number matches the intended numeral; <span class="ex">-teen</span> and <span class="ex">-ty</span> sound different; a phone number is read digit by digit; and a joined number is written with its hyphen.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Reflect</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Explain the choice</h3>
    <p>Complete this aloud: “For 13–19 I use the ending ______. For the tens like 30, 40, 50 I use the ending ______. The loud part of <strong>thirteen</strong> is at the ______; the loud part of <strong>thirty</strong> is at the ______.”</p>
    <p>Then spell two tricky numbers from memory: <strong>40</strong> and <strong>90</strong>. Say one true number sentence about your life right now.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Great. You can read, say, and spell numbers 0–100, and tell -teen from -ty.">
    <h3>Final quiz: numbers in real situations</h3>
